    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the full test suite passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 0 failures).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the **no-future-date** rule for `POST /api/owners`: a supplied `registrationDate` later than the server's current date is now rejected with HTTP 400, following the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions.\n\n**New files:**\n- `ValidateOwnerRegistrationDate.java` \u2014 a validation step that reads the bound DTO (`@Val OwnerFieldsDto`) and throws when a *present* `registrationDate` is after `LocalDate.now()`. An absent date is left alone (it defaults to the server date downstream in `BuildOwner`/`BusinessDays`).\n- `FutureRegistrationDateException.java` \u2014 a checked escalation (`extends Exception`).\n- `FutureRegistrationDateExceptionHandler.java` \u2014 responds 400 with a `ProblemDetail`, mirroring the existing `InvalidPostcodeExceptionHandler`.\n- `officefloor/escalation/\u2026FutureRegistrationDateException.yml` \u2014 wires the exception to its handler.\n\n**Modified:**\n- `owners.POST.yml` \u2014 inserted the `validateRegistrationDate` step right after `validate` (so it runs on the already-bound body, before loads/quota checks), keeping it under the same `transaction` governance as the rest of the pipeline.\n\nI mirrored the existing \"validate-when-present\" pattern used for postcode validation, so the change is consistent with the surrounding code.",
